; factorial using recursion, conditionals, arithmetic, and binding
; A function named fact is defined with one argument, n.
; It returns 1 when n is 0 (the base case of the recursion).
; Otherwise, it multiplies n by the factorial of n - 1.
(fact : (λ (n) (if (= n 0) 1 (* n (fact (- n 1))))))

; Evaluate the factorial of 5.
(↓ (fact 5))

; The previous expression evaluates to 120.
(↓ 120)
